  "receiver_rules": [
    "Every machine surface requires existing pinned backend, manage_options, exact Dashboard and no delegated staff scope. Readiness is global metadata, never individual access or execution permission.",
    "Readiness is acquired fresh over authenticated existing connection: observed_at <= now, expires_at > now and expires_at <= observed_at+30; exact provider source/policy/dependency/map pinned. ready requires current internally consistent approved coherence epoch. Disabled/blocked never source-select or bind. Coherent but owner-disabled status may report coherence_ready:true with a verified epoch while both preview/binding flags remain false; it still cannot source-select or bind.",
    "The public v1 preview schema and v1 delegation remain byte-compatible. Only server source selects the new private original lifetime after coherent readiness. A review shape cannot prove private protocol; exact successful bind/read projection must independently match original local mapping and provider retained state.",
    "Bind/read use unchanged exact original-authorization-v2 claims, role/purposes and 60-second control ceiling. A new original-source context includes the coherence epoch; old originals cannot be upgraded or rebound.",
    "Successful bind projection remains bound-blocked with production/admission flags false. It is not a fresh current-access veto, QA report, backup, approval, source provenance or execution grant.",
    "Read consumes request/nonce history, so it is not marked idempotent or read-only. Lost bind responses recover with a new signed read and the immutable original anchor; never automatically retry a bind.",
    "No controller registration, service startup, allowlist expansion or production activation before provider coherence, source qualification, reviewed configuration and existing deployment gates. Later site writes retain exact preview/QA/backup/approval/CAS/readback/rollback.",
    "Enforce fixed per-call input/output byte, freshness and monotonic deadline limits independently of schemas; a failed, expired or unknown outcome is not retried. Existing content/package/capture/source limits are unchanged."
  ],
